course: dictionary
lesson: 15805
title: Unbelted: a word with three parts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Look at a long word in parts. Un- means not, belt is something you wear to hold on, and -ed shows it describes a person or thing. So unbelted means not wearing a belt. «The little boy sat unbelted in the back of the car, so Dad pulled over.» Car, seat and pulled over are the clues, so unbelted must mean not wearing a seat belt.
explain: Always ask what word would fit. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The little boy sat not wearing a seat belt in the back of the car» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: A word can also mean without a belt, not only in a car. «Her unbelted coat flapped in the wind» means her coat had no belt tied round it. The words around the word, like coat and flapped, tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means "not", as in «unhappy» and «unlocked».
fact: «Unbelted» means not wearing a seat belt in a car or other vehicle.
fact: «Unbelted» can also mean without a belt, such as «an unbelted coat».
fact: Unbelted passengers are much more likely to be badly hurt in a crash, so always wear your seat belt.
exercise: «The little boy sat unbelted in the back of the car.» What does unbelted mean? | *Not wearing a seat belt | Sleeping soundly | Happy to be going on holiday | Wearing a red belt
exercise: «She wore an unbelted dress, so it hung loose at the waist.» What does unbelted mean here? | Dirty and torn | Not wearing a seat belt in a car | *Without a belt | Wearing two belts
exercise: Which word is the opposite of unbelted, meaning wearing a seat belt? | *Belted | Unhappy | Unwell | Unlocked
exercise: The news said, «Unbelted passengers are much more likely to be badly hurt.» What is the warning? | Belts are too tight to wear | Crashes are always funny to watch | *Being unbelted in a vehicle can be dangerous | Passengers should always sit in the front
test: «Mrs Green checked that every child was belted before the bus left, because unbelted children are at risk in a crash.» What does the sentence tell us? | *Unbelted children are in danger if there is a crash | Buses have no seats | Children should never ride on a bus | Belts make a bus go faster
test: Which sentence uses unbelted to mean without a belt, not in a car? | The passengers were unbelted and nervous. | *Her long, unbelted coat flapped in the wind. | Ben forgot his seat belt, so he was unbelted. | Dad sat unbelted in the front seat.
exam: Read: «Mrs Green checked that every child was belted before the bus left, because unbelted children are at risk in a crash.» What does unbelted mean, and why does the author include it? | Happy and playing games on the bus | Wearing a belt with a shiny buckle | *Not wearing a seat belt, so the children could be badly hurt in a crash | Sleeping on the bus during the trip
